{%- comment -%}
  LBASS — pSEO H1 / RATE NOTES (2026-08-04)
  Documentation only. The logic is INLINE in templates/page.pseo.liquid,
  because {% render %} has an isolated scope and could never reassign ps_h1.

  ── WHAT CHANGED AND WHY ──

  1. H1 NOW FOLLOWS page.title.
     Each pSEO page hardcoded its heading:
         assign ps_h1 = 'سنيكرز second-hand أصلية فالمغرب'
     On 2026-08-03 the nine page TITLES were rewritten to informational
     framing ("دليل: كيفاش تختار…") so the collections could own the
     transactional query. The hardcoded H1s did not move, leaving every page
     promising a guide in the <title> and delivering a category in the <h1>.
     Verified live: title "دليل: كيفاش تختار صبابط…" vs h1 "سنيكرز second-hand
     أصلية فالمغرب".

     One line after the case block now does it for all nine:
         {%- if page.title != blank -%}{%- assign ps_h1 = page.title -%}{%- endif -%}

     The hardcoded values stay as fallbacks, so a page with no title still
     renders. And because ps_h1 also feeds the breadcrumb, the WhatsApp
     prefill, BreadcrumbList and CollectionPage schema, all of those follow
     the Admin title automatically from now on. No more hardcoded headings.

  2. SHIPPING 40 → 30.
     Verified shipping is 20 MAD inside Marrakech and 40 MAD elsewhere in
     Morocco (free at 500 MAD).
     This template still said 40 in four places — the Darija answer block, the
     French mirror, the visible FAQ, and the FAQ JSON-LD — plus the trust chip
     that renders on EVERY pSEO page. Schema stating a wrong price is worse
     than body copy doing it, because it is machine-read as fact.

  3. COLLECTION LINKS.
     Parent links use the currently published /collections/nike and
     /collections/adidas-originals handles. Do not repoint them to unpublished
     /brand-* resources; those were verified 404 on 2026-08-20.
{%- endcomment -%}
